  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling-up the Health Response to the Resurgence of Cholera in Haiti</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to reduce morbidity and mortality related to cholera in active hotspots and limit the spread of the disease to other communities. This WHO project 1) provides cholera culture diagnosis capacity to 5 laboratories, 2) monitors/evaluates 12 cholera treatment centers (CTC) with clinical management quality and 3) treats approximately 3,000 suspected cholera patients in the CTCs. The project provides life-saving assistance to 42,000 people, including 12,351 women, 11,862 men, 17,787 children, and 1,681 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
